{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Java 8 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++11 code to Java 8 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++11 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\n\ntypedef bitset<128> u99;\n\nconstexpr const int mod = 1000000007;\nconstexpr const int inv = 570000004;\nconstexpr int add(int a, int b) { return a + b < mod ? a + b : a + b - mod; }\nconstexpr int sub(int a, int b) { return a < b ? a - b + mod : a - b; }\nconstexpr int mul(int a, int b) { return 1LL * a * b % mod; }\n\nmap<u99, int> name;\nint n, dfn, son[65536][128];\nint dfs(u99 s) {\n    auto ite = name.find(s);\n    if (ite != name.end()) return ite->second;\n    int ret = dfn++;\n    name[s] = ret;\n    for (int i = 0; i != (1 << n); ++i) {\n        u99 t = s;\n        for (int j = 0; j != (1 << n); ++j) if (!t[j])\n            for (int k = i & j; k; k ^= k & -k) if (s[j ^ k & -k]) {\n                t[j] = 1;\n                break;\n            }\n        son[ret][i] = dfs(t);\n    }\n    return ret;\n}\n\nint p[7][7], q[7][128], dp[8][65536];\n\nint main() {\n    cin >> n;\n    dfs(1);\n    for (int i = 0; i != n; ++i) for (int j = 0; j != n; ++j) cin >> p[i][j], p[i][j] = mul(p[i][j], inv);\n    for (int i = 0; i != n; ++i) for (int j = 0; j != (1 << n); ++j) {\n        q[i][j] = 1;\n        for (int k = 0; k != n; ++k) q[i][j] = mul(q[i][j], j >> k & 1 ? p[k][i] : sub(1, p[k][i]));\n    }\n    dp[0][0] = 1;\n    for (int i = 0; i != n; ++i) for (int j = 0; j != dfn; ++j) for (int k = 0; k != (1 << n); ++k)\n        dp[i + 1][son[j][k]] = add(dp[i + 1][son[j][k]], mul(dp[i][j], q[i][k]));\n    u99 res;\n    for (int i = 0; i != (1 << n); ++i) res[i] = 1;\n    cout << dp[n][name[res]] << endl;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    static final int MOD = 1000000007;\n    static final int INV = 570000004;\n    \n    static int add(int a, int b) {\n        int s = a + b;\n        return s < MOD ? s : s - MOD;\n    }\n    \n    static int sub(int a, int b) {\n        return a < b ? a - b + MOD : a - b;\n    }\n    \n    static int mul(int a, int b) {\n        return (int)((long)a * b % MOD);\n    }\n    \n    static int n, dfn;\n    static int[][] son;\n    static HashMap<BitSet, Integer> name = new HashMap<>();\n    \n    static int dfs(BitSet s) {\n        Integer idx = name.get(s);\n        if (idx != null) return idx;\n        int ret = dfn++;\n        name.put((BitSet)s.clone(), ret);\n        int limit = 1 << n;\n        for (int i = 0; i < limit; ++i) {\n            BitSet t = (BitSet)s.clone();\n            for (int j = 0; j < limit; ++j) {\n                if (!t.get(j)) {\n                    int mask = i & j;\n                    while (mask != 0) {\n                        int lowbit = mask & -mask;\n                        if (s.get(j ^ lowbit)) {\n                            t.set(j);\n                            break;\n                        }\n                        mask ^= lowbit;\n                    }\n                }\n            }\n            son[ret][i] = dfs(t);\n        }\n        return ret;\n    }\n    \n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        n = sc.nextInt();\n        int limit = 1 << n;\n        son = new int[65536][limit];\n        BitSet init = new BitSet(128);\n        init.set(0);\n        dfs(init);\n        \n        int[][] p = new int[n][n];\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n            for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j) {\n                p[i][j] = sc.nextInt();\n                p[i][j] = mul(p[i][j], INV);\n            }\n        }\n        \n        int[][] q = new int[n][limit];\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n            for (int j = 0; j < limit; ++j) {\n                q[i][j] = 1;\n                for (int k = 0; k < n; ++k) {\n                    if ((j >> k & 1) == 1) {\n                        q[i][j] = mul(q[i][j], p[k][i]);\n                    } else {\n                        q[i][j] = mul(q[i][j], sub(1, p[k][i]));\n                    }\n                }\n            }\n        }\n        \n        int[][] dp = new int[n + 1][65536];\n        dp[0][0] = 1;\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n            for (int j = 0; j < dfn; ++j) {\n                for (int k = 0; k < limit; ++k) {\n                    int val = mul(dp[i][j], q[i][k]);\n                    dp[i + 1][son[j][k]] = add(dp[i + 1][son[j][k]], val);\n                }\n            }\n        }\n        \n        BitSet res = new BitSet(128);\n        for (int i = 0; i < limit; ++i) res.set(i);\n        System.out.println(dp[n][name.get(res)]);\n    }\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [0.0, 0.0, -5.7338023907504976e-05, -2.4199192921514623e-05, -5.960462772236497e-07, -0.0009282094542868435, -0.03905365616083145, -0.00034421717282384634, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.013111800886690617, -0.0024780300445854664, -2.0861407392658293e-05, -0.0011938833631575108, -4.172316494077677e-06, -1.9073468138230965e-06, -5.8410845667822286e-05, -2.3841855067985307